{#
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════
  YOUR PAGE — the organisation's own donation page, edited · /org?tab=page
  ══════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════════

  The editor for `/giving/{slug}`. Everything it writes is `OrgBrand`'s, and that service
  shipped COMPLETE AND UNREACHABLE: a validated writer, a route, an uploader, a provider
  allowlist, contrast refusal, fourteen switchable sections, twelve links, six videos and
  nine two-field blocks — with no form anywhere that posted to it, and (since 3 Oct) no
  console to put one in. §17 and §18 in one feature: every piece correct in isolation and
  nobody ever handed it.

  ── EVERY FIELD NAME IS DERIVED, NEVER TYPED ────────────────────────────────

  `OrgBrand::save()` reads `link_label[]`/`link_url[]`, `video_url[]`/`video_title[]`,
  `section_{key}` for each `SECTIONS` key, and `{block}_{spec.a}[]`/`{block}_{spec.b}[]` for
  each `BLOCKS` entry — and `blockFrom()` derives those last two from the same table this
  template loops. So the names come from `brand_blocks` and `brand_sections`, passed by the
  controller for exactly this reason (its own comment says so).

  Typing them here would be two lists claiming the same thing in the same words, and the
  failure is SILENT: a field named `impact_figures` posts happily, is never read, and the
  organisation saves, sees no error, and finds the block empty.

  ── IT WORKS WITH NO JAVASCRIPT, WHICH IS WHY THE ROWS ARE BLANK ────────────

  Repeating rows arrive as parallel arrays, zipped by index, and a row left half-filled is
  dropped rather than saved as a fragment. So each list draws what is saved plus two empty
  rows: with scripting off that is how an organisation adds one. `OrgBrand` caps each list
  and refuses past it with a sentence, so the cap is stated here rather than discovered.

  ── AND EMBEDS ARE CLICK-TO-LOAD, WHICH IS A LEGAL LINE AND NOT A PREFERENCE ─

  An iframe present in the markup sends the visitor's IP to YouTube or Vimeo and lets them
  set storage on page VIEW, before the visitor has done anything — which under the GDPR
  joint-controller line and the NDPA 2023 needs a lawful basis, and "the page contained a
  video" is not one. The organisation pastes an address, only the video ID is kept, and
  `OrgBrand::embedUrl()` builds ours from a fixed per-provider prefix. Nothing typed here
  ever reaches an `src`. That is also why the provider list is closed: anything else would
  mean running somebody else's code on a page that takes money.
#}

{% if not can_edit %}
  <p class="org-empty__b">{{ 'Only an account owner can edit this page.'|trans }}</p>
{% endif %}

<form class="org-ed" method="post" action="/org/brand" enctype="multipart/form-data">
  <input type="hidden" name="_token" value="{{ csrf_token }}">

  {# ── WHERE IT LIVES ──────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <p class="org-ed__where">
    {{ 'Your page is at'|trans }}
    <a href="/giving/{{ org.slug }}">africagates.org/giving/{{ org.slug }}</a>
  </p>

  {# ── THE LOOK ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <fieldset class="org-fs">
    <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ 'The look'|trans }}</legend>

    <div class="org-row">
      <label class="org-lab" for="brand-accent">{{ 'Your colour'|trans }}</label>
      <input class="org-swatch" type="color" id="brand-accent" name="accent"
             value="{{ brand.accent }}"{% if not can_edit %} disabled{% endif %}>
      {#
        It is refused if it cannot be read on white, with the measured ratio in the message.
        Said here rather than only on rejection: this colour paints the donate button and
        every link, so a pale one leaves a donor unable to see them.
      #}
      <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Colours your donate button and links. It must be readable on white.'|trans }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="org-row">
      <label class="org-lab" for="brand-logo">{{ 'Your logo'|trans }}</label>
      {% if brand.logo %}
        <img class="org-logo" src="{{ asset('/' ~ brand.logo) }}" alt="" width="120" height="48">
      {% endif %}
      {% if uploads_on %}
        <input class="org-file" type="file" id="brand-logo" name="logo"
               accept="image/png,image/jpeg,image/webp"{% if not can_edit %} disabled{% endif %}>
      {% else %}
        <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Uploads are unavailable here, so the logo cannot be changed.'|trans }}</p>
      {% endif %}
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  {# ── THE WORDS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <fieldset class="org-fs">
    <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ 'What you say'|trans }}</legend>

    <div class="org-row">
      <label class="org-lab" for="brand-tagline">{{ 'One line about the work'|trans }}</label>
      <input class="org-in" type="text" id="brand-tagline" name="tagline"
             value="{{ brand.tagline }}" maxlength="{{ brand_max_tagline }}"
             placeholder="{{ 'Books and a reading room for every child in Ọ̀wọ̀'|trans }}"
             {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
      <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Up to %n% characters. It sits under your name, above the form.'|trans({'%n%': brand_max_tagline}) }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="org-row">
      <label class="org-lab" for="brand-story">{{ 'Your story'|trans }}</label>
      <textarea class="org-in org-in--tall" id="brand-story" name="story" rows="8"
                maxlength="{{ brand_max_story }}"
                {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>{{ brand.story }}</textarea>
      <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Separate paragraphs with a blank line. Switch the story block on below.'|trans }}</p>
    </div>

    <div class="org-row">
      <label class="org-lab" for="brand-website">{{ 'Your website'|trans }}</label>
      <input class="org-in" type="url" id="brand-website" name="website" inputmode="url"
             value="{{ brand.website }}" placeholder="https://"
             {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
      {#
        The address they typed into a field labelled as public — never `contact_email`,
        which is the compliance contact given to verify a CAC registration and is not a
        press office.
      #}
      <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Published on your page. Switch the contact block on below.'|trans }}</p>
    </div>
  </fieldset>

  {# ── WHAT APPEARS ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Every one of the fourteen, as a checkbox, in the service's own order. A block with
     nothing in it draws nothing even when it is switched on, so the switch is about intent
     and the content below decides whether there is anything to show. #}
  <fieldset class="org-fs">
    <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ 'What appears on the page'|trans }}</legend>
    <ul class="org-switches">
      {% for key, what in brand_sections %}
        <li class="org-switch">
          <input type="checkbox" id="sec-{{ key }}" name="section_{{ key }}" value="1"
                 {% if brand.sections[key]|default(false) %}checked{% endif %}
                 {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
          <label for="sec-{{ key }}">{{ what|trans }}</label>
        </li>
      {% endfor %}
    </ul>
  </fieldset>

  {# ── LINKS ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <fieldset class="org-fs">
    <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ 'Links'|trans }}</legend>
    <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Up to %n%. Give every link a few words saying what it is.'|trans({'%n%': brand_max_links}) }}</p>

    {% set lrows = brand.links|default([]) %}
    {% for i in 0..(lrows|length + 1) %}
      {% set row = lrows[i]|default(null) %}
      <div class="org-pair">
        <input class="org-in" type="text" name="link_label[]" maxlength="{{ 90 }}"
               value="{{ row ? row.label : '' }}"
               aria-label="{{ 'What the link is'|trans }}"
               placeholder="{{ 'Our 2026 annual report'|trans }}"
               {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
        <input class="org-in" type="url" name="link_url[]" inputmode="url"
               value="{{ row ? row.url : '' }}"
               aria-label="{{ 'The web address'|trans }}" placeholder="https://"
               {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </fieldset>

  {# ── VIDEO ───────────────────────────────────────────────────────────── #}
  <fieldset class="org-fs">
    <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ 'Video'|trans }}</legend>
    <p class="org-hint">
      {{ 'Paste the address from %p%. Up to %n%. Nothing loads until a visitor presses play.'|trans({
        '%p%': brand_video_names|join(' ' ~ 'or'|trans ~ ' '),
        '%n%': brand_max_videos}) }}
    </p>

    {% set vrows = brand.videos|default([]) %}
    {% for i in 0..(vrows|length + 1) %}
      {% set row = vrows[i]|default(null) %}
      <div class="org-pair">
        <input class="org-in" type="text" name="video_url[]" inputmode="url"
               value="{{ row ? org_watch_url(row) : '' }}"
               aria-label="{{ 'The video address'|trans }}"
               placeholder="https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=…"
               {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
        <input class="org-in" type="text" name="video_title[]" maxlength="90"
               value="{{ row ? row.title|default('') : '' }}"
               aria-label="{{ 'What the video is'|trans }}"
               placeholder="{{ 'The day the borehole arrived'|trans }}"
               {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
      </div>
    {% endfor %}
  </fieldset>

  {# ── THE NINE BLOCKS ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
     Impact figures, the gift ladder, quotes, the FAQ, the team, the history, the partners —
     whatever `OrgBrand::BLOCKS` holds, with its own labels, hints, caps and row limit. Add
     a block to that table and it appears here; nothing in this file names one. #}
  {% for name, spec in brand_blocks %}
    <fieldset class="org-fs">
      <legend class="org-fs__l">{{ brand_sections[name]|default(name)|trans }}</legend>
      <p class="org-hint">{{ 'Up to %n% rows. A row missing either part is left out.'|trans({'%n%': spec.max}) }}</p>

      {% set rows = brand.blocks[name]|default([]) %}
      {% for i in 0..(rows|length < spec.max ? rows|length + 1 : spec.max - 1) %}
        {% set row = rows[i]|default(null) %}
        <div class="org-pair">
          <input class="org-in org-in--a" type="text"
                 name="{{ name }}_{{ spec.a }}[]" maxlength="{{ spec.a_max }}"
                 value="{{ row ? row[spec.a]|default('') : '' }}"
                 aria-label="{{ spec.a_label|trans }}" placeholder="{{ spec.a_hint }}"
                 {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
          <input class="org-in" type="text"
                 name="{{ name }}_{{ spec.b }}[]" maxlength="{{ spec.b_max }}"
                 value="{{ row ? row[spec.b]|default('') : '' }}"
                 aria-label="{{ spec.b_label|trans }}" placeholder="{{ spec.b_hint }}"
                 {% if not can_edit %}disabled{% endif %}>
        </div>
      {% endfor %}
    </fieldset>
  {% endfor %}

  {% if can_edit %}
    <button class="org-go org-go--wide" type="submit">{{ 'Save your page'|trans }}</button>
  {% endif %}
</form>
